The Home of the Future.

I interviewed in Redmond for a visual designer contract role. It turned out to be for Microsoft’s Home of the Future, an experimental space with a kitchen, living room and bedrooms, where they would showcase technology opportunities. These were near-term, in the next 3-5 years, and meant to spark conversation more than prove feasibility. Each season they would curate an update and I worked with PM’s to help realize it.

It introduced me to Microsoft and I was impressed with the scope and possibility of what they were trying to realize. That first contract was about 6 months but I was invited back for another year with SBG, Startup Business Group. Getting the opportunity to work with researchers, developers and PM’s who were at the top of their game was rewarding and huge learning experience. Even though Microsoft wasn’t in a good place for design (the iPad had just launched) they were filled with smart, driven folks.

After that year I was asked to interview for a role. I interviewed with both SBG and Xbox; my manager at SBG had just accepted a role at Xbox. The videogame connection combined with user experience design at Xbox was an amazing opportunity and I was thrilled to accept a full-time role in February of 2011.

